// Quran topics: two bundled sources, merged by exact Arabic topic name.
// NOTHING here is fetched at runtime — the app works fully offline.
//
// Source 1 — Quranpedia.net (https://quranpedia.net), dump version
// 2026-11-14, schema /v1/ayah/{surah}/{ayah}/topics. Free to use inside
// apps with no attribution required (a link is appreciated); republishing
// the data itself as a downloadable dataset requires crediting
// Quranpedia.net. This is the DETAILED taxonomy (4,576 topics, 799 parent
// topics) — but upstream classified only surahs 1-39 (plus one ayah each
// in surahs 52, 58, 62, 74, 88). A fresh dump (version 2026-11-21, checked
// 2026-11-22) has the IDENTICAL 1-39 coverage, so Quranpedia alone cannot
// complete surahs 40-114.
//
// Source 2 — Quranic Universal Library (QUL) topics, via the
// Quran-Tajweed-Engine (https://github.com/TheAbubakrAbu/Quran-Tajweed-Engine,
// MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Abubakr Elmallah; data extracted, with
// attribution, from the open-source Al-Islam app). The QUL ayah-topics
// dataset itself is otherwise only downloadable behind a sign-in on
// quran-universal-library; this copy comes from the open MIT-licensed
// repackaging. Of its 2,512 topics only the 991 with a non-empty Arabic
// name and >= 1 ayah are used here — the rest are English-only taxonomy
// nodes / index fragments with no Arabic name, or parent categories with
// 0 ayahs, so they cannot be shown in this Arabic UI. QUL topics are a
// BROADER taxonomy than Quranpedia's (concepts like «الله»، «فرعون»),
// not the same fine-grained one.
//
// Merge (build-topics-108.py, 1.0.108): a QUL topic whose Arabic name
// exactly equals a Quranpedia topic name is merged into that entry (union
// of ayah refs, source "both"); other QUL topics are new entries
// (id 100000 + QUL id, parentId null — different taxonomy, no Quranpedia
// parent — source "qul"). Entries with no `source` field are Quranpedia.
// All ayah refs are sorted numerically and de-duplicated; the list stays
// sorted by ayah count descending.
//
// COVERAGE (verified at build time): topics now exist for ALL 114 surahs
// (QUL covers every surah; Quranpedia covers 1-39 in detail). See also
// src/data/surah-sections.ts — per-surah topic outlines for 111 surahs
// (surahs 1, 42, 44 have no section outline in that source).

